{"reasoning": "Instruction alignment description:
出现新的机械臂去夹盘子，

指令要求将餐具从右水槽移至左水槽，所有餐具始终未离开右水槽，目标完全未达成", "instruction_alignment": 2}

{"reasoning": "Instruction alignment description:
动作主体匹配 存在问题：指令要求仅使用右夹爪操作，视频中左夹爪也参与了物品抓取，动作主体使用存在偏差

目标完成度 部分完成：仅少量目标物品被放入蓝色托盘，大部分白色圆柱罐和白色袋装物仍留在原托盘，未完全达成分拣目标", "instruction_alignment": 3}

{"reasoning": "1) Agent match: The same two robotic grippers/arms visible in the first frame perform all actions throughout the frames; no agent switch occurs.

2) Object correctness: The left gripper interacts with the silver metal bowl that initially sits on the orange plate (it grasps and lifts it off the plate). The right gripper interacts with the yellow sponge on the green tray (it grasps and lifts the sponge).

3) Goal completion: The instruction requires manipulating the silver bowl with the left gripper and the yellow sponge with the right gripper. Both manipulations occur: the left gripper picks up and moves the bowl off the orange plate toward the left side of the table, and the right gripper picks up and moves the sponge (bringing it toward the center/left and later returning it near the green tray). By the end, both target objects have been actively manipulated by the specified grippers, satisfying the goal.", "instruction_alignment": 5}

{"reasoning": "1) Agent match: The same white robot arm/gripper visible in the first frame is present throughout and is the only manipulator interacting with the scene.

2) Object correctness: The instruction requires moving small brown fruits/vegetables into the left bowl on the stovetop, then moving remaining small red fruits/vegetables into the silver right bowl (sink). In the frames, the robot moves near the stovetop burners and the sink area, but there is no clear grasp-and-place of any small brown items into a left bowl. The only clearly visible target-like object is a small red item near/inside the sink; it appears in the sink area later, but the frames do not show a clear pickup and placement action by the gripper.

3) Goal completion: By the end, there is no evidence that the small brown items have been placed into the left bowl on the stovetop, and the “remaining small red” items are not clearly collected into the right (sink) bowl either (only one red item is visible in/near the sink, with no demonstrated sorting of all items). Overall the instructed two-stage sorting task is not achieved.", "instruction_alignment": 2}

{"reasoning": "1) Agent match: The same overhead robotic manipulator/gripper visible in the first frame performs all interactions throughout the sequence; no agent switch is observed.

2) Object correctness: The instruction targets a white mug and a yellow-and-white mug. The video shows the robot mainly manipulating a gray/white mug (placing it onto plates) while the yellow mug remains off the plates (hovering/right side) and the blue/white mug stays behind it; there is no clear placement of a distinct “yellow and white” mug onto the right plate.

3) Goal completion: By the end, there are mugs on both plates, but they appear to be the same gray/white mug duplicated/teleported rather than (a) the white mug on the left plate and (b) the yellow-and-white mug on the right plate. The yellow mug is not placed on the right plate, and the specified final arrangement is not achieved.", "instruction_alignment": 2}
